{
  "_comment": "Prompt ID migration map — Handoff 11 (tech debt round).",
  "date": "2026-08-21",
  "reason": "The es-/pt-/en- prefix originally meant \"target language\" but drifted to mean \"origin set\" once prompts became multi-target (a prompt with an es- prefix may be drillable in English). The prefix carried a claim that was no longer true. New convention is {category}-{NNN}: the category segment is stable and carries no false claim. practiceAsTarget is, and always was, the authoritative signal for what is drillable in which language — the ID is just a stable identifier. Numbers follow the order prompts appeared in prompts.json at migration time, and are never reused after a deletion.",
